%% Rust for Tauri — full flow
%% Pure Mermaid. No Markdown fence.

flowchart TD
    trigger([Writing Rust in src-tauri]) --> what{What is being added?}

    what -->|A command| cmd
    what -->|Shared state| state
    what -->|Startup work| setup
    what -->|A dependency| dep

    cmd{Does it wait on IO?}
    cmd -->|yes| async[async fn — take OWNED params<br/>&str is not supported directly]
    cmd -->|no| sync[Plain fn]

    async --> blocking{Does it do CPU-heavy<br/>or blocking work?}
    blocking -->|yes| spawn[tauri::async_runtime::spawn_blocking<br/>otherwise the runtime stalls]
    blocking -->|no| errors
    spawn --> errors
    sync --> errors

    errors[Return Result, never panic —<br/>a panic can take down the PROCESS<br/>where a JS exception would be caught]
    errors --> errtype{Does a serialisable<br/>error type exist?}
    errtype -->|no| make[thiserror enum + manual Serialize<br/>use #from so ? works]
    errtype -->|yes| lock
    make --> lock

    state[app.manage in setup — no Arc needed]
    state --> mutex{Is it read from an<br/>ASYNC command?}
    mutex -->|yes| tokio[tokio Mutex — .lock await<br/>a std guard held across await deadlocks]
    mutex -->|no| stdm[std::sync::Mutex]
    tokio --> lock
    stdm --> lock

    setup[.setup hook: seed state, open a db,<br/>register a tray, start background work<br/>Err here means the app will not start]
    setup --> lock

    dep[Minimal features:<br/>default-features = false + what you need]
    dep --> size[Watch lib.rs size —<br/>split into src/commands/ modules<br/>before the 500-line ceiling]
    size --> lock

    lock{cargo fmt --check<br/>cargo clippy -- -D warnings}
    lock -->|fails| fix[Fix, then re-run]
    fix --> lock
    lock -->|passes| done([Done: no panics, correct locking, lint-clean])

    classDef gate fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#d97706,color:#7c2d12
    classDef terminal fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b
    class what,cmd,blocking,errtype,mutex,lock gate
    class trigger,done terminal
